From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:58:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: HFI gen2 features and fixes for VA-API

Xilin Wu, "[PATCH 0/5] media: iris: HFI gen2 features and fixes for
VA-API" v1, <20261029-iris-va-fixes-v1-0-44a2783f782b@radxa.com>,
patches 2-5 squashed. They make qcom-va-driver work on gen2:

2/5 media: iris: allow larger capture buffer pools on HFI gen2
    <20261029-iris-va-fixes-v1-2-44a2783f782b@radxa.com>
3/5 media: iris: Add deblocking filter controls for HFI gen2
    <20261029-iris-va-fixes-v1-3-44a2783f782b@radxa.com>
4/5 media: iris: Preserve timestamps on error buffers
    <20261029-iris-va-fixes-v1-4-44a2783f782b@radxa.com>
    Reviewed-by: Bryan O'Donoghue <bryan.odonoghue@linaro.org>
5/5 media: iris: Recycle decoder buffers for non-display pictures
    <20261029-iris-va-fixes-v1-5-44a2783f782b@radxa.com>

1/5 (decode-order output on gen2, Ack Nicolas Dufresne) is NOT taken:
1092 adds the same two controls and the same HFI_PROP_DECODE_ORDER_OUTPUT,
sent only once a client sets them, to inst_fw_cap_sm8550_dec, the
decoder table of every gen2 SoC novadeck ships. 1/5 also covers Milos,
which no board uses.

Bodies identical, except 5/5's last hunk in
iris_hfi_gen2_handle_output_buffer(), placed by hand: 1102 had already
widened the zero-size error check to PSC_LAST. 5/5 rewrites that check as
buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST, which iris_hfi_gen2_get_driver_buffer_flags()
sets for both LAST and PSC_LAST, so 1102's behaviour is kept.

Review on the list (open as of 2026-11-21): 2/5, why decoder-only and why
not keep the maximum in the platform data; 5/5, fluster results asked
for. Bryan O'Donoghue, 2026-11-17: "close to mergable".

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
---
